<!--
  The settings: a window of their own, opened from File > Settings (spec/10-platforms.md:
  "a settings page or dialog"). spec/06-library.md, "Settings", has them in sections:
  Chords, the colour of a chord in each of the two editors, and Backups, the copies
  that are kept, all of them.

  It is opened over the app's window and is to be closed before that is gone back to.
  Nothing in it changes a song. A colour chosen in it is how the app draws chords from
  then on, and the window behind it shows it at once; what it shows of the copies is as
  they were when it was opened.

  A window only frames what is in it. What is in it is a view of its own (SettingsView),
  put in by the code beside this, so that a test can draw it into a picture.
-->
<Window x:Class="Pro7ChordEditor.AppViews.SettingsWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        Title="Settings"
        Width="960"
        Height="600"
        MinWidth="760"
        MinHeight="440"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" />
